{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe remote gate is refs/reconciler/gate. Older binaries require a non-empty gated_mode string and fail closed on unknown formats. Retiring the mode ladder therefore needs an additive, rollback-safe blob rather than a new-only schema. The writer retains gated_mode: reconcile-check while adding paused, reason, who, and paused_at. A vendored verbatim pre-change decoder must accept every new blob. Old mutating reconcile modes keep blocking on gated_mode; the read-only reconcile-check path remains allowed because __main__.py returns through _run_reconcile_check before check_phase_gate, and that ordering must remain unchanged.\n\nThere is no duration or automatic expiry. An --until field would diverge old and new readers and could silently unpause only part of a fleet, so it is explicitly out of scope. Pause remains active until an operator resumes it.\n\nThe existing set_gate and clear_gate ref writers already use expected-old-oid CAS. Pause and resume preserve that mechanism: a rejected CAS is surfaced as a clean conflict with the re-read remote state; it is never retried blindly or allowed to clobber another operator.\n\nPause provenance is deterministic. who is the repository git config user.email resolved by git config --get user.email; pause refuses without writing when it is missing or blank and does not fall back to the OS user. paused_at is generated in UTC RFC3339 form only for the first successful pause. An idempotent same-reason re-pause preserves the stored who and paused_at exactly.\n\nA live error-path bug crosses the same seam: check_phase_gate runs before the reconciler try block today, so a corrupt gate escapes as a traceback. Move the mutating-mode gate read inside the protected path while preserving the earlier reconcile-check return. Corrupt state emits recovery guidance and returns clean exit 1. Do not rename check_phase_gate in this ticket.\n\n## Operator and workflow behavior\n\n- rebar bridge pause REASON requires a nonblank reason and writes the additive dual-format blob.\n- Pausing an already-paused bridge is idempotent only when the requested reason matches; it reports the existing pause without changing who or paused_at. A different reason refuses with the current remote state.\n- rebar bridge resume clears the gate through the same CAS seam. Resuming an unpaused bridge exits 0 with a notice.\n- Missing origin refuses loudly; CAS conflict exits nonzero with the re-read remote state; corrupt state exits 1 with recovery guidance.\n- A new paused gate blocks mutating reconciler modes as a benign exit 0 and emits one stable machine-readable line beginning BRIDGE_PAUSED: followed by the reason and provenance. This is distinct from both the existing legacy gated_mode-only throttle path and corrupt-state failures. This leaf does not rewrite the legacy gate exit mapping.\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml preserves every existing rc mapping. On rc 0 it captures and replays reconciler output, emits a GitHub notice only when the exact BRIDGE_PAUSED: marker is present, and otherwise retains the converged message. Nonzero corrupt and legacy gate outcomes still reach the generic error arm.\n\n## Compatibility and test plan\n\nUse expand-contract ordering: additive reader and dual-format writer ship together. Feed every new blob to a vendored verbatim pre-change decoder; prove gated_mode remains a real legacy Mode member. Through the real bridge CLI and temporary git repositories, exercise first pause, blank reason, missing git email, already-paused same and different reasons, unpaused resume, missing remote, CAS conflict, corrupt blob, and exact remote ref state. Assert metadata stability and unrelated-state preservation. Exercise the old rebar reconcile --mode entrypoint against the new blob: mutating modes remain blocked for old readers, while reconcile-check still takes its pre-gate early return. Exercise the workflow with paused marker, ordinary rc 0, every existing benign rc, corrupt rc 1, and legacy gate rc 4 so only a genuine new pause becomes a notice. No test asserts private names or source layout.\n\nSurface parity census:\n- CLI command: in scope through real rebar bridge pause/resume subprocess tests.\n- MCP or API tool: out of scope because pause/resume are intentionally operator-only writes in this story; the persisted format compatibility is tested at the shared ref seam.\n- Library facade: out of scope for the same operator-only boundary; existing reconcile library behavior is unchanged.\n- Automated callers: in scope through the scheduled workflow contract and real legacy reconcile entrypoint.\n- Dual direction: in scope; pause writes and blocks, resume clears and restores mutation, with exact remote state asserted.\n\nNo new contention harness is needed: each operator action is one existing expected-old-oid CAS operation, not a composed check-then-act outside that seam. The deterministic conflict test proves the operation does not retry or overwrite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every new gate blob carries paused, reason, who, paused_at and retains gated_mode: reconcile-check.\n- [ ] who is repository git user.email; missing identity refuses without a write; paused_at is first-pause UTC RFC3339 and same-reason re-pause preserves both fields exactly.\n- [ ] A vendored pre-change decoder accepts every blob the new writer emits, and real legacy reconcile coverage proves mutating modes stay blocked while reconcile-check preserves its pre-gate early return.\n- [ ] rebar bridge pause REASON and rebar bridge resume are the only new supported write path; old reconcile vocabulary and existing gate readers remain functional.\n- [ ] Blank reasons are rejected; same-reason re-pause is idempotent without metadata loss; different-reason re-pause refuses; resume while unpaused is a successful notice.\n- [ ] Existing expected-old-oid CAS protects pause/resume, and a conflict surfaces current remote state without blind retry or overwrite.\n- [ ] A genuine new pause blocks mutating bridge work with exit 0 and the exact BRIDGE_PAUSED: marker; corrupt state returns clean exit 1 with recovery guidance; existing legacy gate exit behavior is unchanged.\n- [ ] Pause detects a missing remote and refuses rather than reporting local-only success.\n- [ ] The scheduled workflow notices only the BRIDGE_PAUSED: rc-0 outcome and preserves ordinary success, legacy benign, corrupt, and generic error mappings.\n- [ ] No --until, automatic expiry, new-only blob value, check_phase_gate rename, or old-vocabulary removal ships."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786208078730413001,"uuid":"1922ae7e-224a-4f48-82b0-8a5d9a0d80af"}